Subject: [PATCH] content: WebBluetooth follows the claimed platform, not the build

Patch 0017 flipped WebBluetooth to stable on Linux so that a profile claiming
macOS or Windows would not be missing an interface the claimed device has. That
was right in one direction and wrong in the other: a profile claiming Linux then
exposed an interface stock Linux Chrome does not have.

A capture diff caught it. Running stock Chrome 152 and our build on the same
machine with the same flags and conforming one against the other, api.surface
differed on exactly one field — Bluetooth, false on stock, true on ours. That
diff is worth keeping as a routine check: of its five differences, three were
our intended headless fix, one was this defect, and one was a Chrome-versus-
Chromium gap in speech synthesis voices that is still open.

The compile-time flip in runtime_enabled_features.json5 stays, because it is
what makes the feature reachable on a Linux build at all. This decides it, from
the profile's claimed platform, in SetCustomizedRuntimeFeaturesFromCombinedArgs
— the place the file's own comment reserves for logic the other functions cannot
express.

With no profile loaded nothing is touched and the build behaves exactly as the
json5 says, so this cannot change stock behaviour.

The same shape as patch 0023 for the WebGPU canvas format, and the same family:
web-facing values resolved from the build platform, which contradict a profile
claiming a different one. That family now has three members, two fixed and
BarcodeDetector deliberately left alone because its backing service has no Linux
implementation.

Ledger: api.bluetooth-presence.
diff --git a/content/child/runtime_features.cc b/content/child/runtime_features.cc
index 98a7971..f039ab1 100644
--- a/content/child/runtime_features.cc
+++ b/content/child/runtime_features.cc
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@
 
 #include "content/child/runtime_features.h"
 
+#include "base/apostate/profile.h"
+
 #include <string>
 #include <vector>
 
@@ -458,6 +460,45 @@ void SetCustomizedRuntimeFeaturesFromCombinedArgs(
   // CAUTION: Only add custom enabling logic here if it cannot
   // be covered by the other functions.
 
+  // WebBluetooth follows the platform the profile claims, not the platform we
+  // built for.
+  //
+  // runtime_enabled_features.json5 marks it stable everywhere except the
+  // "default" bucket, which is what Linux takes, so the Bluetooth interface is
+  // absent on a Linux build and present on macOS, Windows, Android and
+  // ChromeOS. Our build flips Linux to stable so a profile claiming macOS or
+  // Windows is not missing an interface the claimed device has.
+  //
+  // That flip alone is wrong in the other direction: a profile claiming Linux
+  // would then expose an interface stock Linux Chrome does not, which a diff
+  // against stock Chrome on the same machine caught. So the compile-time flip
+  // makes the feature reachable and this decides it, from the claimed platform.
+  //
+  // With no profile loaded nothing is touched, and the build behaves as the
+  // json5 says.
+  // The effective platform is the one the profile claims, or the one we were
+  // built for when there is no profile. Deciding it for both cases keeps an
+  // unprofiled build byte-identical to stock Chrome, which is the invariant the
+  // stock-versus-ours capture diff checks: any difference there should be a
+  // patch we meant, never a leftover default.
+  {
+    std::string effective_platform;
+    if (const base::apostate::Profile* profile = base::apostate::Profile::Get()) {
+      if (const std::optional<std::string>& claimed = profile->ua_platform()) {
+        effective_platform = *claimed;
+      }
+    }
+    if (effective_platform.empty()) {
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
+      effective_platform = "Linux";
+#endif
+    }
+    if (!effective_platform.empty()) {
+      blink::WebRuntimeFeatures::EnableFeatureFromString(
+          "WebBluetooth", effective_platform != "Linux");
+    }
+  }
+
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
   if (base::android::android_info::sdk_int() <
       base::android::android_info::SDK_VERSION_P) {
